.TH "Docv" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv \- src/docv/crystal_pages/pages.cr
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
src/docv/crystal_pages/pages.cr
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.PP
\fBVERSION\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.base_directory(variable : String, fallback : String) : String\fR
An XDG base directory: \fB\%$variable\fR, or \fB\%\(ti/fallback\fR when the variable is
unset or not an absolute path.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.find(name : String, section : String | Nil = nil, manpath : Manpath = Manpath.default) : String | Nil\fR
Finds the file of page \fIname\fR in \fIsection\fR along \fImanpath\fR
(\fB\%Manpath.default\fR: the added directories and the system path).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.load(path : String, options : Options = Options.new) : Document\fR
Reads and parses the file at \fIpath\fR (plain or gzip): Markdown when it is
named like a Markdown document (\fB\%Markdown.file?\fR), roff otherwise.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.open(name : String, section : String | Nil = nil, manpath : Manpath = Manpath.default, options : Options = Options.new) : Document | Nil\fR
Finds and parses page \fIname\fR; \fB\%nil\fR when there is no such page.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse(text : String, path : String | Nil = nil, options : Options = Options.new) : Document\fR
Parses roff source \fItext\fR. \fIpath\fR is the file it came from, used to
resolve \fB\%.so\fR includes; \fIoptions\fR enables unsafe requests.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.user_directory(variable : String, fallback : String) : String\fR
This program\(aqs directory under an XDG base directory: \fB\%$variable/docv\fR,
or \fB\%\(ti/fallback/docv\fR when the variable is unset or not an absolute
path.
